["For fixed tau>0, N006 gives Dinv:L^2->H^1 and the H^1 algebra bound. Thus Ftau is a continuous quadratic L^2->H^1 map. The first Htau term is a product of two inverse derivatives followed by P. The second uses the continuous bilinear mean P0(f^2), bounded by ||f||_2^2. The third has an H^1 cubic product followed by Dinv. The fourth has Dinv2 Ftau(f) and Dinv f, again an H^1 product followed by Dinv2; all coefficients, including tau^(-1), are finite for fixed tau. Hence Psi_tau is continuous from mean-zero L^2 to L^2. Every output is mean-zero: the first and third/fourth corrections have P or an inverse derivative; the mean of the second term is zero because Dinv f has zero mean. Conjugate Fourier symmetry and the real coefficients give reality. Smoothness is preserved by these operations, so finite smooth trajectories exist without any bound on their higher norms.",["N006"],[],[["F001","At each fixed positive tau the displayed Scheme is a continuous real mean-zero L^2 map and preserves smoothness."]]],
["For any smooth input f at grid step n, identify source exp(t*partial_x^3) with S_(-t). The source Ftau,Htau formulas are exactly D008, term by term, with coefficients 1/6,1/3,tau/9,-1/54,-1/(27*tau), and identical endpoint signs. The source inverse derivative and mean have the same multipliers. In the twist, S_(-(t_n+tau))Ftau(S_(t_n)f)=F_(t_n)(t_n+tau;f,f), also following from N006's endpoint formula. The source cubic remainder has alpha=3ab(a+b), beta=3kc(a+b), the covariance eta and the prefactor -tau/(18ik), exactly R2. E005 therefore yields f_(n+1)=f_n+F_n(t_(n+1))+C_n(t_(n+1))-R2^n_tau(f_n,f_n,f_n). Substitution in Interp makes Q_n(t_(n+1)) cancel with its part of W_n; hence V(t_n)=f_n and V(t_(n+1))=f_(n+1).",["E005","N006"],["F001"],[["F002","For smooth Scheme trajectories the interpolation matches both step endpoints and the source remainder is exactly R2, with the sign in D021."]]],
["Endpoint matching gives continuity across all grid points; all ingredients are spatially smooth and piecewise time-smooth. On a step F_n'=B_t(f_n,f_n)/2, C_n'=B_t(f_n,F_n), Q_n'=B_t(F_n,F_n)/2. Thus V'=B_t(z_n,z_n)/2-W_n/tau. Since V=z_n+Y_n, expansion gives V'=B_t(V,V)/2-B_t(Y_n,z_n)-B_t(Y_n,Y_n)/2-W_n/tau. The last three terms are precisely rho_n' and hence mathcalR' on that step. The concatenation is continuous at its endpoints and starts at zero. The mean and reality properties follow from F001 and the real, mean-zero operators used throughout. Quantify the smooth trajectory and fixed tau to obtain N007.",[],["F001","F002"]]
],
[{id:"A001",input:"E005",at:"S002",bindings:"Source vn=f_n=S_(-t_n)U^n, source F^n=F_(t_n) from Stage, source A^n=C_n(t_(n+1)), source R2^n=R2_(t_n,tau). Source scheme (1.4)=D008.",hypothesis_checks:["The paragraph considers a smooth mean-zero f_n, at tau>0 and n>=0; F001 ensures such Scheme iterates exist.","The termwise comparison of the fixed update and the Airy twist identifies the exact source scheme, with no cutoff or convergence assumption."]}]);
