ype","value":"error path"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/kind","value":"definition"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/declaration","value":"Set e=v-V."},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/objects/0","value":"v"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/objects/1","value":"V"},{"path":"/inference/locals/10/symbol","value":"E_I"},{"path":"/inference/locals/10/type","value":"error supremum"},{"path":"/inference/locals/10/declaration","value":"Set E_I=sup_I||e||_2."},{"path":"/inference/locals/11/symbol","value":"N"},{"path":"/inference/locals/11/type","value":"real threshold"},{"path":"/inference/locals/11/kind","value":"arbitrary"},{"path":"/inference/locals/11/declaration","value":"Fix N as specified in this proof."},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/symbol","value":"g"},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/type","value":"midpoint path"},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/start","value":"S001"},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/end","value":"S005"},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/declaration","value":"Set g=v-e/2."},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/objects/0","value":"v"},{"path":"/inference/locals/12/objects/1","value":"e"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/symbol","value":"Fint"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/type","value":"integrated quadratic error"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/start","value":"S001"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/end","value":"S005"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/declaration","value":"Set Fint(t)=integral_a^t B_s(e,g)ds."},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/objects/0","value":"a"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/objects/1","value":"e"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/objects/2","value":"g"},{"path":"/inference/locals/13/objects/3","value":"B"},{"path":"/inference/locals/14/symbol","value":"Lcut"},{"path":"/inference/locals/14/type","value":"low projection"},{"path":"/inference/locals/14/kind","value":"definition"},{"path":"/inference/locals/14/declaration","value":"Set Lcut=P_(<=N/3)."},{"path":"/inference/locals/15/symbol","value":"Hcut"},{"path":"/inference/locals/15/type","value":"high projection"},{"path":"/inference/locals/15/kind","value":"definition"},{"path":"/inference/locals/15/declaration","value":"Set Hcut=identity-Lcut, where identity is the identity Fourier operator."},{"path":"/inference/locals/16/symbol","value":"f1"},{"path":"/inference/locals/16/type","value":"first generic time path"},{"path":"/inference/locals/16/declaration","value":"Fix arbitrary f1 with the domain and conditional premises specified in this paragraph."},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/symbol","value":"f2"},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/type","value":"second generic time path"},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/start","value":"S003"},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/end","value":"S003"},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/declaration","value":"Fix arbitrary f2 with the domain and conditional premises specified in this paragraph."},{"path":"/inference/locals/17/objects/0","value":"<removed>"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/symbol","value":"f3"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/type","value":"third generic time path"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/start","value":"S003"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/end","value":"S003"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/kind","value":"arbitrary"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/declaration","value":"Fix arbitrary f3 with the domain and conditional premises specified in this paragraph."},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/from_inputs/0","value":"<removed>"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/objects/0","value":"<removed>"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/objects/1","value":"<removed>"},{"path":"/inference/locals/18/objects/2","value":"<removed>"},{"path":"/inference/argument/2/text","value":"For any three qualifying paths f1,f2,f3, put Lcut=P_(<=N/3), Hcut=identity-Lcut. The trilinear telescoping expansion is C(f1,f2,f3)-C(Lcut f1,Lcut f2,Lcut f3)=C(Hcut f1,f2,f3)+C(Lcut f1,Hcut f2,f3)+C(Lcut f1,Lcut f2,Hcut f3). The all-low product has no output above N. Projections contract both parts of X, while ||Hcut fj||_(H^(-pstar))<=C*N^(-pstar)||fj||_2. In each expanded term apply N002 with the negative norm on its specified high input. Hence ||P_(>N)C_[a,t](f1,f2,f3)||_2<=C*h*product||fj||_X+C*N^(-pstar)*product||fj||_(L^infty L^2). Apply this to (e,g,V) and (v,v,e). N009 yields ||e||_X<=C_M*(tau^gamma+E_I) and bounds the other X norms by C_M; the product of L^2 norms contains E_I. Their total is therefore <=C_M*h*tau^gamma+C_M*(h+N^(-pstar))*E_I."},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/text","value":"For the forcing term, on each intersected step use the actual residual formula N007: integral J(mathcalR',V)=-C(Y_n,z_n,V)-C(Y_n,Y_n,V)/2-tau^(-1)integral J(W_n,V). The intervals here are the completed or partial intersection with the step. The first two are O_M(tau*q_n) by N002, putting its negative norm on Y_n, using N008's ||Y_n||_X<=C_M*q_n and ||Y_n||_(H^(-pstar))<=C_M*tau*q_n, ||z_n||_X<=C_M, and N009's bounded V norm on the intersection. H002 and 0<tau<=1 give tau^gamma<=1; since delta_n<=E_I<=1, q_n<=2 and q_n^2<=2*q_n. The last term is O_M(tau*q_n) by N008's ||W_n||_2<=C_M*tau*q_n and the L^2 J bound from N006, since the intersection length is <=tau. Every intersected step starts in I, so delta_n<=E_I. There are at most h/tau+1 such steps. Summing bounds the entire forcing term, also after P_(>N), by C_M*(h+tau)*(tau^gamma+E_I)."},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/0","value":"H002"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/1","value":"N002"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/2","value":"N006"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/3","value":"N007"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/4","value":"N008"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/uses/5","value":"N009"}]}
{"candidate":19,"inference":"R011","definitions_checked":["D001","D002","D003","D004","D005","D006","D007","D008","D009","D010","D011","D013","D014","D015","D016","D017","D019","D020","D021"],"unchanged_mathematical_fields_omitted":true,"changes":[{"path":"/inputs/4/statement","value":"There is an absolute C>0 such that the following bounds hold uniformly in time. For mean-zero f,g in L^2 and all real t, ||Dinv f||_(H^1)+||Dinv f||_infinity<=C||f||_2, ||B_t(f,g)||_(H^(-pstar))<=C||f||_2||g||_2, ||J_t(f,g)||_(H^1)<=C||f||_2||g||_2, and ||Dinv P(fg)||_2<=C||f||_2||g||_2. For mean-zero A, ||A||_(H^(-pstar))<=||Dinv A||_2 whenever the latter is finite; ||J_t(A,g)||_2<=C||Dinv A||_2||g||_2. For all A,A2 in H^1, the algebra bound is: ||A*A2||_(H^1)<=C||A||_(H^1)||A2||_(H^1). S_t is unitary in every H^s, preserves reality/mean and is strongly continuous. For continuous, piecewise time-smooth spatially smooth mean-zero paths f,g on [a,b], integral_a^b B_t(f,g)dt=(1/3)[J_t(f,g)]_a^b-(1/3)integral_a^b[J_t(f',g)+J_t(f,g')]dt. Also J_t is symmetric and integral_I J_t(B_t(f,g),h)dt=C_I(f,g,h). In particular F_a(t;f,g)=[J_s(f,g)]_(s=a)^(s=t)/6 for constant inputs. All bounded product maps extend from polynomials by density."},{"path":"/inputs/5/statement","value":"For each fixed tau>0, Psi_tau from Scheme is a continuous polynomial map from mean-zero L^2 to mean-zero L^2, preserving reality; Ftau maps L^2 continuously to H^1. Smooth data produce smooth iterates. For any trajectory produced by Scheme from smooth mean-zero data, f_n=S_(-t_n)U^n, the Interp construction has V(t_n)=f_n, V(t_(n+1))=f_(n+1), is continuous and piecewise smooth in time and spatially smooth, and has mean-zero values, which are real whenever the initial datum is real. On each open step, V'=B_t(V,V)/2+mathcalR', where mathcalR'=-B_t(Y_n,z_n)-B_t(Y_n,Y_n)/2-W_n/tau. Thus mathcalR is continuous with the defining increments and the displayed residual identity holds a.e."},{"path":"/inference/locals/6/objects/0","value":"K0"},{"path":"/inference/locals/6/objects/1","value":"N"},{"path":"/inference/locals/7/symbol","value":"Bcount"},{"path":"/inference/locals/7/type","value":"natural block-count bound"},{"path":"/inference/locals/7/declaration","value":"Set Bcount=ceil(2*T/delta)+1."},{"path":"/inference/locals/7/objects/0","value":"T"},{"path":"/inference/locals/7/objects/1","value":"delta"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/symbol","value":"K"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/type","value":"uniform recurrence bound"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/start","value":"S003"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/declaration","value":"Set K=max(1,3*K0*delta*(2^Bcount-1))."},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/objects/0","value":"K0"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/objects/1","value":"delta"},{"path":"/inference/locals/8/objects/2","value":"Bcount"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/symbol","value":"tau0"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/type","value":"positive permitted step bound"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/start","value":"S004"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/declaration","value":"Set tau0=min(1,delta/2,(1/(4*K))^(1/gamma))."},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/objects/0","value":"delta"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/objects/1","value":"K"},{"path":"/inference/locals/9/objects/2","value":"gamma"},{"path":"/inference/locals/14","value":{"symbol":"tstar","type":"real candidate first-hit time","scope":"R011/argument","start":"S004","end":"S004","kind":"arbitrary","declaration":"Under L2 let tstar be the asserted first time with error norm one. If any crossing exists, continuity from e(0)=0 supplies such a time.","from_inputs":[],"from_local":[],"objects":["e","T"]}},{"path":"/inference/argument/1/text","value":"Choose an integer N>=2 so large that K0*(N^(-1)+N^(-pstar))<=1/4; this is possible because pstar>0. Choose delta=min(1,1/[4*K0*(N^2+3)])>0 and restrict tau<=min(1,delta/2). On any grid-start interval with length h<=delta and E_I<=1, the small-frequency and timestep terms obey K0*(N^2*h+h+tau)<=K0*delta*(N^2+3)<=1/4. N010 therefore absorbs at most half of E_I and yields E_I<=2||e(a)||_2+3*K0*delta*tau^gamma. This estimate includes both endpoints and does not require e(a)=0."},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/text","value":"Set tau0=min(1,delta/2,(1/(4*K))^(1/gamma))>0. Assume L4: tau<=tau0. If L2: the error first reached norm one at some time tstar, continuity and e(0)=0 give an error supremum <=1 on [0,tstar]. F003, including its partial-last-block case, then gives ||e(tstar)||_2<=K*tau^gamma<=1/4, a contradiction. Discharge L2; continuity excludes all crossings and yields sup_[0,T]||e||_2<=K*tau^gamma. At grid points N007 gives V(t_n)=S_(-t_n)U^n and N006 gives unitarity, so the grid error equals ||u(t_n)-U^n||_2. Rename K as C, quantify the smooth datum and all L with tau<=tau0, and retain the constants chosen before them. Discharge L4 and L3; this proves the smooth-data estimate, uniformly in spectral support and higher norms."},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/introduces/0","value":"L4"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/introduces/1","value":"L2"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/discharges/1","value":"L4"},{"path":"/inference/argument/3/discharges/2","value":"L3"}]}
